A||N||2||Formula88||Crankshaft pulley size?||||5||
Z||000000||Formula88||11-28-2001||12:48 PM||||Does anyone know the size of the OEM crankshaft pulley on a V6 (88, if it matters)?  I just replaced the alternator and belt on my Formula, but the stock belt won't tighten up enough to stop squealing - and it's at the limit of the alternator's travel.  I'm wondering if maybe it had a power pulley installed sometime before I bought it.  <P>LZeitgeist has an 88 Formula, too, but his doesn't have AC.  Are the crank pulleys the same between AC and non/AC cars?  I could compare mine against his if they're the same.<P>One last question... assuming I do have a power pulley, does anyone know the correct belt length for it?<P>LZ and I have raced in the past, and our Formulas run virtually identical - side by side.  But I've got A/C, he doesn't.  I also weight a lot more than his skinny self.  So I've got probably a 200lb or so disadvantage.  All things being equal, his car should be slightly faster.   A power pully might explain why we run so dead even.  That and I have almost 2x the mileage on my engine as his (120K vs. ~60K) so I wouldn't think my engine's making more power unless it's had some changes.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shaun41178||11-28-2001||01:06 PM||||I dont' remember off hand but I do know that this website gives the dimensions of the stock and underdrive pulley.  In fact it is my website  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS</A> <P>Just look for the link that says underdrive and click on that.  That should have all the info you need I think.<P>hope this helps<P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||11-28-2001||02:01 PM||||Thanks for the info!  I'm reading your page, and it's slightly confusing ... please clarify.<P>"The circumference of the original pulley is 20.5 inches in diameter and the diameter of the new pully is 15inches."   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>I take it you mean it's 20.5" circumference, right?  And the new one is 15" circumference?||||reg||10
